  "body": "## Goal\n\nStep 1, PR A of the UI plan #4245, with #1120 and #4209. The palette of the shell, in dark and light themes, comes from tokens in the kit crate (`crates/ui-kit`). The last colour literals of `crates/ui` move into tokens. Numbers in fields and readouts use a monospace font.\n\n## What is decided (#4245, review of 2026-11-28)\n\nNew tokens, with these values. Each status ink passes 4.5:1 on the window ground (`ink`), the panel ground (`ink_alt`), the well (`well`) and its own fill, in both themes. Each control border passes 3:1 on the grounds it sits on:\n\n| Token | Dark ink / fill | Light ink / fill |\n|---|---|---|\n| `status_ok` | `#6FC793` / `#1B3426` | `#1D6B42` / `#D9EEDF` |\n| `status_warn` | `#FFA24D` / `#3A2A14` | `#9C4A00` / `#F7E6D0` |\n| `status_error` | `#FF7A7A` / `#3E2024` | `#B3261E` / `#F7DEDB` |\n| `status_info` | `#7DB0E6` / `#1C2D40` | `#2F5F92` / `#DDE8F4` |\n| `control_border` (edges of fields, buttons, check boxes) | `#737B88` | `#767E8A` |\n\n- Today's `border` (`#3D434C`) stays for dividers only (1.52:1 on the panel ground is below the 3:1 floor for control edges).\n- Today's warn ink (1.97:1) and error ink (2.65:1) on the light ground fail the 4.5:1 text floor: the new status inks replace them.\n- Height planes and move types get two separate token groups later (PR C1 and C2), not in this PR.\n\n## Order\n\nStart after PR #4466 (#4452, three preview inks in the kit) merges: both PRs edit the kit's theme tables, the legal check, the names, the overlay and the gallery lists.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Each new token is in the theme struct, the dark and light tables, the legal check, the names, the overlay, the gallery lists, `assets/themes/theme.json.example` and `docs/user-guide/themes.md`.\n- The contrast tests of the kit check each new token against the grounds above in both themes.\n- `crates/ui` has no colour literals left outside the allowed list (`theme/verdict.rs` and the documented exceptions). The colour-literal guard test proves it.\n- Numbers in fields and readouts use the monospace font. A test checks the font family of one numeric field.\n- Layout and structural tests updated. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down (#1953). No snapshot PNG changes.\n- Before and after screenshots, dark and light, at 1366×768.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file.\n\nPart of #4245. Does part of #1120 and #4209. Enables PR C1 and PR B.\n",
